  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Carahsoft Technology has $1.5B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Carahsoft Technology received 1,594 awards in the same period, with an average award size of $939K. Carahsoft Technology obligations are down 17.2% year over year. Carahsoft Technology received the largest share of FY2026 obligations from the Department of Defense, which obligated $713M, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services at $233M and the Department of Homeland Security at $142M. Carahsoft Technology remains concentrated in software and IT markets: Software Publishers accounts for $1B and Other Computer Related Services accounts for $241M. Carahsoft Technology obligations by fiscal year show growth into FY24 and FY25 before the current-year partial total: FY21 was $1.2B, FY22 was $1.3B, FY23 was $1.4B, FY24 was $1.8B, FY25 was $1.8B, and FY26 is $1.5B. This snapshot summarizes where federal dollars are flowing to Carahsoft Technology and which agencies and NAICS markets are the primary sources of demand.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Carahsoft Technology's largest federal buyers in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $713M. The Department of Health and Human Services follows with $233M, and the Department of Homeland Security follows with $142M. Additional significant buyers include the Department of Agriculture at $101M and the Social Security Administration at $70.6M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and product types dominate Carahsoft Technology obligations?",
        "body": "Software and IT services dominate Carahsoft Technology obligations, with Software Publishers accounting for $1B and Other Computer Related Services accounting for $241M. Custom Computer Programming Services totals $64.4M and Electronic Computer Manufacturing totals $22.1M. Smaller markets include Research and Development at $11.5M and Computing Infrastructure Providers at $2.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
